One of the pilots you'll be training
is Goose's son.

00:12:37.130 --> 00:12:38.250
Who's Goose?

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:40.040
What? Goose.

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:42.210
The guy you just spent 35 years mourning.

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:43.800
Oh! Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah, Goose.

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:46.720
Yeah, oh, wow, brain toot.

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:48.300
Yeah, thanks for the heads-up.

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:54.810
Welcome to Top Gun: Maverick.

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:57.690
Our mission, destroy
a uranium enrichment plant

00:12:57.690 --> 00:12:59.900
in that unnamed country that is our enemy.

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:01.860
Man, I want to cream those guys!

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:04.190
To complete this mission, I propose we fly

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:06.860
at a low altitude,
undetected through a canyon,

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:08.160
then destroy the target.

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.620
All in under two and a half minutes.
Questions?

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:13.160
Yeah, this mission seems really similar

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:14.620
to the one in Star Wars.

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:16.790
People can fly low and shoot a small thing

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:18.330
without it being a Star Wars.

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:20.040
Yeah, but the text
on the screen even says,

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:21.630
"Womp rat-sized target."

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:23.250
Don't look at the screen.

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:25.510
Any other questions not about Star Wars?

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:27.130
Why'd you kill my dad?

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:29.510
- No more questions!
- Do you do your own stunts?

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:30.760
Well, maybe one more.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:32.140
As a matter of fact, I do.

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:33.260
Had you not heard that?

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:34.640
Anyway, I'm gonna fly the mission.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:36.140
You're all cut except for Goose's son.

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:37.560
So why are we even here?

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:39.310
Only stunt questions from you, Bob.

00:13:39.486 --> 00:13:40.425
I'm Bob?

00:13:50.256 --> 00:13:51.197
Iceman.

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:53.410
Ah, it's good to see you again.

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:55.160
We have so many memories together.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:02.790
Anyway, I need your advice.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:04.170
If I don't pick Rooster for the mission,

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:06.050
he's never gonna forgive me
for everything.

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:07.550
But I'm afraid he's not ready.

00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:08.274
What should I do?

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:32.830
Thanks, Iceman.
I knew you'd know what to do.

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:36.200
So, are you all silent and scarfed
because you're dying?

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:38.000
No, is that what people are saying?

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:40.370
No, I'm just on vocal rest
for karaoke later.

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:42.130
I'm 100% totally fine.

00:14:42.266 --> 00:14:43.466
I've never felt better in my li--

00:14:44.567 --> 00:14:45.920
Aw, he died.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.670
Five miles to target.
Try to keep up, Rooster.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:08.180
Not gonna be a problem.

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:10.260
Let's keep the small talk to a minimum.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:10.783
Got it.

00:15:12.653 --> 00:15:14.773
So, how's your dad doing, good?

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:16.010
You killed him.

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:17.930
Yeah, and I was more than five miles out,

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:20.180
and I could have done anything
with his body, but I didn't.

00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:21.890
Yeah, the more you say that,

00:15:21.890 --> 00:15:23.640
the more I don't think it's true.

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:27.190
Are you angry at me
for pulling your papers

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:28.650
from the Naval Academy?

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:30.520
'Cause I've already
forgiven myself for that.

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:33.360
I had a whole scene with Iceman
and Iceman's computer about it.

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:36.610
This is about everything,
my dad, the papers.

00:15:36.610 --> 00:15:39.320
And why'd you write my mom
out of the sequel?

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:40.410
It's complicated.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:43.330
There's scheduling conflicts
and different creative visions,

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:45.160
and it wouldn't be fair to her

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:47.420
to use her in a way that's
inorganic to the narrative.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:49.960
Inorganic? I should be 40 years old,

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:51.670
but somehow I'm, like, 20?

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:53.300
Oh, people don't care about those details,

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:56.180
as long as you have loud jets
and America kicking ass.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:21.240
That was awesome!

00:16:21.265 --> 00:16:22.855
Hey, let's take a selfie to celebrate.

00:16:24.676 --> 00:16:27.460
This is totally main-feed material.

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:31.040
Maverick, no!

00:16:37.832 --> 00:16:40.292
Oh, no! We lost 'em.

00:16:40.585 --> 00:16:42.015
They's gone, sir.

00:16:43.318 --> 00:16:45.118
Well, I know it's only 12:15,

00:16:45.818 --> 00:16:47.473
but that's all we had to do today, so...

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:50.060
long weekend!

00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:59.530
Aw, one of my AirPods fell out.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.200
Rooster!

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:14.380
Do you think I took that missile

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:15.880
so you could be down here with me?

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:18.010
You should be back at the carrier by now.

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:19.880
I was trying to save you.

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:21.430
No, I was trying to save you.

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:23.720
Look, I'm sorry, Rooster.

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:25.930
For your dad, for pulling your papers,

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:28.430
and for signing you up for
Gavin Newsom's text messages.

00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:31.690
I responded "STOP"
and it just wouldn't stop.

00:17:31.690 --> 00:17:33.900
Why were you doing all these things?

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:35.940
To protect you. At first.

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:37.860
Then I kind of got addicted to the idea

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.950
of controlling every minute
detail of a person's life.

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:45.990
Get down, Mav!

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.160
I also replaced your weapons
with gender reveal things.

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:52.000
That is the last thing, though, I swear.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:55.790
Aw.

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:04.640
Hello, Maverick.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:07.220
You guys are the bad guys? Why?

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:08.560
Why do you think?

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:10.520
We were important parts
of that first movie,

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.640
and you just tossed all the women aside.

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:14.940
Yet you somehow figured out
how to keep in a guy

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:16.560
who's literally unable to speak.

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:19.230
This is all a big misunderstanding,
and I can fix it.

00:18:19.230 --> 00:18:21.320
They're talking about doing
another Jerry Maguire.

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:23.860
How would you like to be
the fat head kid's grandma?

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:26.120
And you can be Minority Report's grandma.

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:27.950
I got grandma parts for all of you.

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:30.580
How come you get to be
a 60-year-old action star

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.040
and we have to be grandmas?

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:33.460
We can do action, too, you know.

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:35.540
And we're gonna prove it right now.

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:38.420
Let me just put on
my reading glasses, hold on.

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:39.412
Wait. You're right.

00:18:39.566 --> 00:18:41.356
You both brought up some painful memories,

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:42.760
or engrams.

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:45.130
What if I told you that,
through a series of audits,

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:47.510
I can help you go clear
and liberate the thetan

00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:49.470
trapped inside your astral shell?

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:51.180
Is that like horoscopes?

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:53.310
It is kind of like stars and space stuff.

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:55.770
Yeah, if you want,
I can go grab an E-meter from my plane.

00:18:55.770 --> 00:18:57.520
You know, I have been feeling a little off

00:18:57.520 --> 00:18:58.900
since the last half-moon.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:00.150
Okay, be quick.

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:06.320
- I can't believe they fell for that crap.
- Oh, yeah, such crap,

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:08.530
definitely not something
I've left two families over.

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:10.990
What are you doing, Mav?

00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:12.540
I'm getting us out of here.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.870
You sure this old thing can even fly?

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:15.960
It's not that old.

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:18.269
Look at its full head
of log cabin brown hair.

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:21.050
I know horoscopes are a little flimflammy,

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:22.970
but people act like
they're fortune cookies...

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.470
Damn it, they're stealing
that very young plane!

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:35.850
We're never gonna lose 'em in this thing.

00:19:47.272 --> 00:19:49.200
We can't take much more of this.

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:50.027
We're gonna have to eject.

00:19:50.106 --> 00:19:52.030
I'm gonna climb,
then we'll eject on three.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:54.200
On three or after three?

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:56.370
You're just like your stupid father.

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:01.300
Take the shot.

00:20:10.550 --> 00:20:12.310
Iceman! He's alive!

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:14.640
Yay! Saved by a guy!

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:32.830
It's good to have my wingman back.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:33.990
I thought we lost you.

00:20:33.990 --> 00:20:35.830
Nope. I'm as healthy as I've ever--

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:37.750
Aw, he died again.

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:41.710
Well, that was pretty fun.

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:43.380
Top Gun: Maverick went on to make

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:45.710
over a billion dollars at the box office.

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:46.651
You know what that means?

00:20:46.762 --> 00:20:48.262
People are going to the movies again.

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:50.130
Isn't that right, Tiny Tom Cruise?

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:52.510
That's right, Peter. Now let's jump!

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:54.260
Why are we jumping again?

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:56.180
So people will watch your stuff,

00:20:56.180 --> 00:20:57.930
and because I don't know
I'm not in a movie

00:20:57.930 --> 00:20:59.560
all the time.

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:01.730
You do your own stunts?

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:03.980
Oh, yeah, were you not aware of that?